  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On rue Jean Aicard in Sainte-Maxime, Le Carillon serves Franco-Italian cuisine (grilled dishes, pizzas) on a terrace, with the relaxed atmosphere typical of this seaside town. The quality of the food is consistently praised across two independent platforms: 4.8/5 on Restaurant Guru (1,127 reviews) and 96% recommended on its Facebook page (44 reviews).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Several independent customer reviews describe a warm welcome for dogs, with one account even mentioning a chair offered for a small dog during a visit. No official rule published by the establishment itself has been found — this confirmation comes only from customer reviews, so take it as a good sign rather than an absolute guarantee. Service runs from 12pm to 2pm and then 7pm to 10pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: ask for a terrace table when you arrive — that's where your dog will be most comfortable.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Sainte-Maxime's town centre and seafront are close to rue Jean Aicard.</p>
